course: dictionary
lesson: 13381
title: Headbutt: a hard hit with the head
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To headbutt means to hit someone or something hard with the top or front of your head. Headbutt can be a verb, as in «The goat headbutted the gate», or a noun, as in «The goat gave the gate a headbutt.»
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The ram lowered its horns and charged at the fence» tells you the ram is about to hit something with its head. Headbutt is made of two smaller words, head and butt, so you can guess it is a hit with the head.
explain: You will meet headbutt in stories and news about fights and football fouls. It is not a friendly move. Hitting someone with your head can hurt them badly, so it is never a safe or fair thing to do.
fact: Headbutt means to hit someone or something hard with the top or front of your head.
fact: A headbutt is the hit itself: «The player's headbutt knocked him to the ground.»
fact: Goats and rams often headbutt, and they can do it to each other.
fact: Headbutting can cause serious head injuries, so never headbutt anyone.
fact: Phrases to know: give someone a headbutt, or headbutt the ball.
exercise: «The goat gave the fence a headbutt.» What does headbutt mean here? | A gentle pat | A loud shout | *A hard hit with the top of its head | A long walk
exercise: «Ravi headbutted the ball into the net.» What did Ravi hit the ball with? | His hand | His foot | His knee | *His head
exercise: In «The ram will headbutt the tree», what kind of word is headbutt? | an adjective | *a verb | a noun
test: What does «The goats headbutt each other» tell you? | *They hit each other hard with their heads | They hug each other | They run away from the field | They sleep under a tree
test: Why is headbutting dangerous? | It is always allowed in games | It makes the ball go faster | *It can cause serious head injuries | It makes you laugh
exam: Which sentence uses headbutt as a noun? | «He will headbutt the wall.» | *«The headbutt made him dizzy.» | «They headbutt each other.»
